Z||000000||starfighter007@msn.com||03-11-2001||07:04 PM||||Ihave 85 fiero 2.8 v-6 5speed plus reverse   that was modified to look like ferrari f40 I bought car about 10 months ago.I feel i am still getting to know my little baby like when I give her a bath I spend 2 to 3 hours drying her masaging her all over inside and outside when I am in her engine compartmentwiping things off and examining everything that I can I keep staring at these two aluminum pipes that are between the valve cover and the luggage compartment these pipes protrude from the luggage compartment they are about a 1 1/4" in diameter they are about 7"long after some butcher cut them and are about 2 feet apart.I am just not sure what they would have been used for in the past?? also by the luggage compartment on the right side rear near yhe top I noticed this small inspection cover.SOOOOOOO I thought I will have a little looksee there is what appears to be a blower motor like for a heater anywhoo could some one enlighten on these things Thanks in  advance JIM Riggio||||reg||11
Z||000001||c m west||03-11-2001||07:09 PM||||the is an electric cooling fan located on the right side of the trunk, these pipes direct air onto the coil and alternator for cooling<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero<BR>www,cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
